ory Conference Services North Manchester Campus Facilities Fort Wayne Campus Facilities Catering & Food Services Lodging Options Conferences & Meetings Retreats & Camps Weddings & Banquets News & Media News Brand Toolkit Media Relations Bring the whole family Homecoming Info for: Future Spartans Current Students Parents & Counselors Faculty & Staff Alumni Home > Academics > Student Success > Career & Professional Development Give Request Info Visit Apply Give Request Info Visit Apply Career & Professional Development Career Ready From Day One Explore Spartan Ready Find Opportunities Meet with Career Development Your Future Career At Manchester University, your future starts before graduation. Through career coaching, experiential learning, internships, employer connections, and the Spartan Ready program, you’ll develop the skills, experiences, and confidence needed to thrive after Manchester. Why Career Readiness Matters More Than a Degree Today’s employers are looking for graduates who can communicate effectively, solve complex problems, adapt to change, collaborate with diverse teams, and apply knowledge in real-world environments. Manchester helps students intentionally develop these competencies throughout their college experience. Based on the Spartan Ready framework and competency model, students are guided to build experiences, reflect on learning, and communicate their value to employers and graduate schools. Hire and MU Student The Spartan Skills Advantage Earn badges and build up your skills to increase your attractiveness to future employers. Enter the workforce with confidence and credible documented experience. Is your skillset ready for today’s competitive job market? Contact Career and Professional Development Location Chinworth Center, Room 103 Monday – Friday 8 a.m. – 5 p.m. (260) 982-5025 Email Us Spartan Ready Experiential Learning Employer Partnerships Handshake Critical Thinking Experiential Learning Exercising Ethical Judgement Complex Problem Solving Oral Communication Analyzing & Interpreting Data Utilizing Technology Written Communication Motivation & Innovation Collaborative Teamwork Cross Culteral Understanding Adaptability & Flexibility View All Spartan Skills The Spartan Ready Journey Four Years. One Purpose. Build Foundations Build Foundations Career Assessments Resume Development LinkedIn Handshake Get Involved Get Involved Campus Employment Organizations Leadership Athletics Gain Experience Gain Experience Internships Research Study Away Micro-Internships Launch Your Future Launch Your Future Portfolio Employer Partnerships Applications Graduate School Planning Explore Opportunities Experiential Learning Learn through internships, research, study away, and applied experiences. Career Preparation Develop professional skills and confidence through coaching and workshops. Employer Connections Meet employers, attend career fairs, and build your network. Spartan Ready Track your growth and prepare for life after Manchester. Engage. Equip. Empower Experiential Learning At Manchester University, learning extends beyond the classroom. Through internships, undergraduate research, study away opportunities, student employment, and other hands-on experiences, students apply what they learn in real-world settings while developing the skills employers and graduate schools value most. Experiential learning helps students build confidence, explore career interests, strengthen professional networks, and gain practical experience before graduation. Whether collaborating with faculty on research, participating in a study away program, completing an internship, or engaging in project-based work, students have opportunities to connect academic knowledge with meaningful professional growth. These experiences often help students develop key career-ready competencies such as critical thinking, communication, teamwork, adaptability, problem solving, and cross-cultural understanding—skills that support success long after graduation. Ready to learn more? Explore Manchester University’s experiential learning opportunities and discover how hands-on experiences can help shape your future. Turn Learning into Experience Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow NORTH MANCHESTER 604 E College Ave. PO Box 365 North Manchester, IN 46962 260-982-5000 FORT WAYNE 10627 Diebold Rd. Fort Wayne, IN 46845 260-470-2700 Request Info Visit Give Apply Refer a student Jobs at Manchester University Book an Event Canvas News Bookstore Events Library Quick Links Recruit Me FERPA Title IX Privacy Policy Nondiscriminatory Policy Annual Security Reports Hazing Policy/Hazing Transparency Report ©2026 Manchester University"
